1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,450
Today, Germany has 84 million people. The UK, just under 70 million.

2
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:11,511
On the United Nations' central projection, Germany starts shrinking,

3
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:13,225
and the UK keeps growing.

4
00:00:14,025 --> 00:00:19,200
In 2059, the lines cross, at about 76 million each.

5
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:25,250
By 2100: the UK, 74 million. Germany, 71.

6
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:30,383
Germany has more immigrants, but more deaths than births. A projection,

7
00:00:30,383 --> 00:00:34,250
not a promise. Our full video explains why the lines bend.
